WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
Autumn, in a synagogue.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.560
Someone lifts a curved
ram's horn and blows.

3
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.580
One long blast.

4
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.380
Three broken notes.

5
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.080
Nine short ones.

6
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.420
The horn opens Rosh
Hashanah, the new year.

7
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:20.070
Ten days later comes Yom Kippur:
25 hours without food or drink.

8
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.590
Why would a new year begin
with ten days of saying sorry,

9
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.620
and end in a fast?

10
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.450
In this mission, you'll find out what
the horn's notes are said to mean,

11
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.310
and taste the new year's sweet foods.

12
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.590
Then you'll follow Yom Kippur from its
first evening service to its final blast.

13
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.900
Your mission: find out why Jews start their
new year with ten days of saying sorry,

14
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.240
ending in a 25-hour fast.
